1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,605
A tiny splinter in your finger

2
00:00:01,625 --> 00:00:03,443
sets off your immune system.

3
00:00:03,529 --> 00:00:04,589
Your skin is a wall

4
00:00:04,609 --> 00:00:06,148
that keeps germs out.

5
00:00:06,235 --> 00:00:07,120
The splinter just

6
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:08,211
punched a hole in it,

7
00:00:08,231 --> 00:00:10,525
and bacteria ride in on the wood.

8
00:00:10,728 --> 00:00:12,124
Damaged cells release

9
00:00:12,144 --> 00:00:13,543
chemical signals.

10
00:00:13,746 --> 00:00:15,758
Nearby blood vessels widen,

11
00:00:15,778 --> 00:00:17,769
so more blood flows in.

12
00:00:17,856 --> 00:00:19,926
That's why the spot turns red,

13
00:00:19,946 --> 00:00:21,612
warm and swollen.

14
00:00:21,699 --> 00:00:23,118
White blood cells squeeze

15
00:00:23,138 --> 00:00:24,152
out of the vessels and

16
00:00:24,172 --> 00:00:25,548
follow the signals.

17
00:00:25,751 --> 00:00:27,983
Neutrophils usually arrive first

18
00:00:28,003 --> 00:00:30,238
and swallow bacteria whole.

19
00:00:30,441 --> 00:00:31,536
Bigger cells called

20
00:00:31,556 --> 00:00:33,533
macrophages eat germs

21
00:00:33,553 --> 00:00:35,057
and clean up the mess.

22
00:00:35,329 --> 00:00:36,926
Often, that's enough.

23
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:38,687
But a dendritic cell also

24
00:00:38,707 --> 00:00:40,266
grabs pieces of the germ and

25
00:00:40,286 --> 00:00:42,205
carries them to a lymph node,

26
00:00:42,225 --> 00:00:44,658
a small bean-shaped station.

27
00:00:45,023 --> 00:00:46,164
There, the pieces are

28
00:00:46,184 --> 00:00:47,512
checked against a huge

29
00:00:47,532 --> 00:00:49,430
crowd of immune cells.

30
00:00:49,703 --> 00:00:50,925
Only a few B cells

31
00:00:50,945 --> 00:00:52,785
fit this exact germ.

32
00:00:52,988 --> 00:00:53,839
When one fits,

33
00:00:53,859 --> 00:00:56,535
it copies itself again and again.

34
00:00:56,808 --> 00:00:58,846
The copies make antibodies,

35
00:00:58,991 --> 00:01:00,619
Y-shaped proteins that

36
00:01:00,639 --> 00:01:02,468
stick to this one germ.

37
00:01:02,741 --> 00:01:04,172
Antibodies travel through the

38
00:01:04,192 --> 00:01:06,578
blood and coat the bacteria.

39
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:08,363
A coated germ is easier for

40
00:01:08,383 --> 00:01:10,026
the eating cells to find.

41
00:01:10,229 --> 00:01:10,952
The first time,

42
00:01:10,972 --> 00:01:12,313
this takes days.

43
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,564
But some B cells stay

44
00:01:13,584 --> 00:01:15,413
behind as memory cells.

45
00:01:15,686 --> 00:01:17,036
If the same germ comes back,

46
00:01:17,056 --> 00:01:17,779
the response is

47
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:19,337
faster and stronger.

48
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:20,298
That's the idea

49
00:01:20,318 --> 00:01:21,528
behind vaccines.

50
00:01:21,548 --> 00:01:22,318
Back at your finger,

51
00:01:22,338 --> 00:01:23,212
the fight is over,

52
00:01:23,232 --> 00:01:25,328
and the wall is whole again.

